translation.enterpriseNetworking.description	Perforce, proxy routing (proxyrouter) and git routing for this enterprise. The Perforce switch, the proxy routing editor, the proxyrouter egress switches, each dedicated tenant's Perforce proxy switch and each git connection's extra proxies make changes; everything else on this page is read-only.
translation.enterpriseNetworking.perforceTitle	Perforce
translation.enterpriseNetworking.perforceStateEnabled	Enabled
translation.enterpriseNetworking.perforceStateDisabled	Disabled
translation.enterpriseNetworking.perforceStateMixed	Partially enabled
translation.enterpriseNetworking.perforceDescriptionDedicated	Perforce needs two things to be on: the perforce-connections Unleash flag for this enterprise and the p4proxy sidecar on each of its dedicated tenants.
translation.enterpriseNetworking.perforceDescriptionShared	This enterprise runs on the shared tenant, so only the perforce-connections Unleash flag applies. The p4proxy sidecar runs only on dedicated SaaS and VPC tenants.
translation.enterpriseNetworking.perforceFlagOn	perforce-connections flag: on
translation.enterpriseNetworking.perforceFlagOff	perforce-connections flag: off
translation.enterpriseNetworking.perforceSidecarStatus_one	p4proxy sidecar: on for {{on}} of {{count}} dedicated tenant
translation.enterpriseNetworking.perforceSidecarStatus_other	p4proxy sidecar: on for {{on}} of {{count}} dedicated tenants
translation.enterpriseNetworking.perforceSidecarNotApplicable	p4proxy sidecar: does not apply (shared tenant)
translation.enterpriseNetworking.perforceMixedHint	Only part of Perforce is on. It works only when the flag and every dedicated tenant’s sidecar are on.
translation.enterpriseNetworking.perforceLoadFailed	Failed to load the Perforce state: {{error}}
translation.enterpriseNetworking.perforceSwitchAriaLabel	Enable Perforce for this enterprise
translation.enterpriseNetworking.perforceTurnOff	Turn everything off
translation.enterpriseNetworking.perforceReadOnly	Read-only: changing this needs the account settings admin grant.
translation.enterpriseNetworking.perforceConfirmTitle	Confirm Perforce change
translation.enterpriseNetworking.perforceConfirmEnableDedicated_one	You are about to enable Perforce for this enterprise: the perforce-connections flag is turned on for it, then the p4proxy sidecar on its dedicated tenant. Hypervisors pick up the sidecar within about a minute.
translation.enterpriseNetworking.perforceConfirmEnableDedicated_other	You are about to enable Perforce for this enterprise: the perforce-connections flag is turned on for it, then the p4proxy sidecar on its {{count}} dedicated tenants. Hypervisors pick up the sidecar within about a minute.
translation.enterpriseNetworking.perforceConfirmEnableShared	You are about to enable Perforce for this enterprise by turning the perforce-connections flag on for it. It runs on the shared tenant, so there is no p4proxy sidecar to turn on.
translation.enterpriseNetworking.perforceConfirmDisableDedicated_one	You are about to disable Perforce for this enterprise: the p4proxy sidecar on its dedicated tenant is turned off, then the enterprise is removed from the perforce-connections flag. Running Perforce sessions will lose access within about a minute.
translation.enterpriseNetworking.perforceConfirmDisableDedicated_other	You are about to disable Perforce for this enterprise: the p4proxy sidecar on its {{count}} dedicated tenants is turned off, then the enterprise is removed from the perforce-connections flag. Running Perforce sessions will lose access within about a minute.
translation.enterpriseNetworking.perforceConfirmDisableShared	You are about to disable Perforce for this enterprise by removing it from the perforce-connections flag. It runs on the shared tenant, so there is no p4proxy sidecar to turn off.
translation.enterpriseNetworking.perforceEnabled	Perforce enabled for this enterprise
translation.enterpriseNetworking.perforceDisabled	Perforce disabled for this enterprise
translation.enterpriseNetworking.perforceFlagStillEnabled	Removed this enterprise from the perforce-connections flag, but other rules in Unleash may keep it on. Check Unleash.
translation.enterpriseNetworking.perforceUpdateFailed	Perforce update failed: {{error}}
translation.enterpriseNetworking.readOnly	Read-only
translation.enterpriseNetworking.perforceStateLabel	Perforce for this enterprise:
translation.enterpriseNetworking.perforceDetails	Details
translation.enterpriseNetworking.egressTitle	Git and MCP egress through the proxyrouter
translation.enterpriseNetworking.egressDescription	Unleash flags that send this enterprise's git and MCP traffic from Cognition's pods through the proxyrouter on its dedicated tenant, so the tenant's proxy routes apply to it. They act only on tenants with proxy routing configured.
translation.enterpriseNetworking.egressGitHint	Git connections created from now on get the proxyrouter hop. Existing connections keep their proxy chain.
translation.enterpriseNetworking.egressMcpHint	MCP requests from the webserver and the brain go through the proxyrouter after the FRP hop. This changes live traffic.
translation.enterpriseNetworking.egressNotTargetable	This flag isn't tagged field-enable in Unleash, so it can't be changed here.
translation.enterpriseNetworking.egressMetadataUnavailable	Unleash can't be reached for this flag's tags, so it can't be changed here.
translation.enterpriseNetworking.egressLoadFailed	Failed to load the egress flags: {{error}}
translation.enterpriseNetworking.egressConfirmTitle	Confirm egress flag change
translation.enterpriseNetworking.egressConfirmEnable	You are about to enable <code>{{flag}}</code> for this enterprise.
translation.enterpriseNetworking.egressConfirmDisable	You are about to disable <code>{{flag}}</code> for this enterprise.
translation.enterpriseNetworking.git.title	Git routing
translation.enterpriseNetworking.git.description	How this enterprise's VMs reach its git hosts. Hover a value for its raw details.
translation.enterpriseNetworking.git.howItWorks	How git routing works
translation.enterpriseNetworking.git.howItWorksHypervisor	A clone or git provider API call from a VM first reaches the gitproxy on the tenant's hypervisor. The tenant's git traffic setting decides whether gitproxy fetches from the host directly, through an HTTP proxy, or hands the request to git-manager.
translation.enterpriseNetworking.git.howItWorksGitManager	git-manager reaches each host through the tenant's FRP tunnel, then the connection's extra proxies (or the tenant's TENANT_EXTRA_PROXIES when the connection has none). Gateway hostnames go through the proxy routing hop on the tenant's hypervisors ({{proxyrouter}}), which forwards to the gateway.
translation.enterpriseNetworking.git.loading	Loading…
translation.enterpriseNetworking.git.loadFailed	Failed to load git routing: {{error}}
translation.enterpriseNetworking.git.tenantsTitle	Tenants
translation.enterpriseNetworking.git.tenantsDescription	Where this enterprise's VMs run, and how each tenant sends git traffic.
translation.enterpriseNetworking.git.connectionsTitle	Git connections
translation.enterpriseNetworking.git.connectionsDescription	The git hosts this enterprise connects to, and the route git-manager takes to reach each one.
translation.enterpriseNetworking.git.gatewaysTitle	Gateways
translation.enterpriseNetworking.git.gatewaysDescription	Devin Gateways enrolled for this account. Git connections to a routed hostname go through the gateway.
